{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetL8kB44NkkusoBjVfHx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear understanding of the testing requirements. Let me complete the analysis:\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses (`ConflictException`, `ResourceNotFoundException`)\n- Centralized error codes in `ErrorCode` enum\n- Error envelope: `ApiError` with `error.code`, `error.message`, `error.fields`\n- HTTP status mapping: `ConflictException` → 409, `ResourceNotFoundException` → 404, `CREATED` → 201\n- MockMvc tests assert both HTTP status AND response body JSON\n- Tests re-read state after mutations via separate GET requests (verified by skill)\n- Simple in-memory repository pattern\n\n**Affected files** — required changes:\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add `POST /{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that implements the state transition logic\n2. `ApiError.kt` — Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` error code (required for 409 refusal case)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests covering all four scenarios (CREATED→CONFIRMED, already CONFIRMED, CANCELLED rejection, not found)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if the controller is incorrectly modified\n- Adding an error code that doesn't align with naming patterns (must check existing codes)\n- Not implementing idempotency correctly for already-confirmed shipments\n- Forgetting to re-read state after mutations in tests\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket is clear on all four scenarios and expected HTTP statuses.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` error code to the enum. This represents attempting to confirm a cancelled shipment (409 Conflict).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new POST method handler for `/{shipmentId}/confirm`:\n   - Find the shipment by ID; throw `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) if not found\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` code (409)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, update it to `CONFIRMED` and save\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, do nothing (idempotent — no update needed, just return current state)\n   - Return the shipment with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED` — POST to confirm, assert 200 and body shows CONFIRMED, then GET to re-read and verify persistence\n   - `repeated confirm of already CONFIRMED succeeds and changes nothing` — Create and confirm, then confirm again, assert 200 both times, then GET to verify status is still CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment` — Create, write CANCELLED directly to repo (as comment notes this is how fixture sets up terminal state), POST to confirm, assert 409 and error code, then GET to verify status unchanged\n   - `rejects confirming a nonexistent shipment` — POST to confirm non-existent ID, assert 404 and error code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- I considered using a service layer (`ShipmentService`) to handle the state transition logic, but the existing architecture has controllers working directly with repositories (see `OrderController` and `ShipmentController`). Adding a service layer would be unrelated refactoring outside scope.\n- I considered a generic `INVALID_STATE` error code, but since the ticket only names `CANCELLED` as the conflict case, `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` is more specific and follows the existing `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`, `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Throw | Response |\n|------|-------|------|-------|-------|----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId | repository.findById() | repository.save(copy with CONFIRMED) | none | 200 + Shipment JSON |\n| Already CONFIRMED | shipmentId | repository.findById() | none (copy still has CONFIRMED) | none | 200 + Shipment JSON |\n| CANCELLED shipment | shipmentId | repository.findById() | none | ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANCELLED) | 409 + ApiError |\n| Not found | shipmentId | repository.findById() → null | none | ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) | 404 + ApiError |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Confirm CREATED shipment — verify endpoint returns 200 with CONFIRMED body, then GET to verify persistence\n- Test 2: Confirm already CONFIRMED — verify both calls return 200 with CONFIRMED, GET to verify status unchanged\n- Test 3: Confirm CANCELLED shipment — verify endpoint returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code, GET to verify status still CANCELLED (unchanged)\n- Test 4: Confirm non-existent shipment — verify endpoint returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1537,"cache_read_input_tokens":20577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1537},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42488800-a8d4-488b-b853-48f2a8e69887","uuid":"32e2cfca-ea59-495a-88e5-bc30ddd4d1b6","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:22:27.840Z","request_id":"req_011CetL8jYbdUKppDMJvM3s2"}
